- op: create  # c500
  at: '2026-05-17T02:17:06Z'  # c500
  by: agent  # c500
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c500
  clock: 1  # c500
  nonce: c500  # c500
  data:  # c500
    kind: invariant  # c500
    title: "HTTP linker creates kind=function Symbols for HTTP call sites with verb-prefixed URL names (18 nodes on self-analysis, 1 in production)"  # c500
    status: violated  # c500
    priority: 2  # c500
    parent:  # c500
    tags:  # c500
    - linker  # c500
    - http  # c500
    - schema  # c500
    - self_analysis  # c500
    - dogfooding  # c500
    isbefore: []  # c500
    duplicate_of: []  # c500
    not_duplicate_of: []  # c500
    pr_ref:  # c500
    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-16 (round 11).**\n\n**Symptom.** The HTTP linker creates Symbol nodes with `kind=\"function\"` for HTTP call sites — `fetch()`, `requests.get()`, etc. — even though these are CALLS to HTTP endpoints, not function definitions. The Symbols use the HTTP verb concatenated with the URL or URL expression as `name`.\n\n**Concrete production case.** `packages/htrac-frontend/public/service-worker.js:54` contains:\n\n```js\nreturn fetch(event.request).then((response) => {\n```\n\nThis becomes a Symbol node in the behavior map:\n\n```python\n{\n    'id': 'packages/htrac-frontend/public/service-worker.js::http_client::54',\n    'name': 'GET event.request',          # ← HTTP verb + JS expression\n    'kind': 'function',                    # ← but it's a CALL, not a function\n    'language': 'javascript',\n    'origin': '',                          # ← empty (INV-sopon family)\n    'meta': {\n        'framework_role': 'http_client',\n        'http_method': 'GET',\n        'raw_url': 'event.request',\n        'url_path': 'event.request',\n        'url_type': 'variable'\n    },\n    'span': {'start_line': 54, 'end_line': 54, ...},\n    'shape_id': None,\n    'signature': None,\n}\n```\n\n**Scale on self-analysis: 18 such nodes.** All with `kind=\"function\"`, `meta.framework_role=\"http_client\"`, `origin=\"\"`. Names include:\n- `GET event.request` (1, production)\n- `GET /api/users`, `POST /api/users`, `DELETE /api/users/1` (literal-URL test fixtures, 14)\n- `GET API_URL`, `POST config.api_url` (variable-URL test fixtures, 3)\n\n**Downstream consequences.**\n\n1. **`hypergumbo dead-code-maybe` flags the production case as dead code.** The `GET event.request` Symbol has zero callers (because nothing CALLS a Symbol whose name is \"GET event.request\"), so dead-code analysis lists it as potentially dead. The actual `fetch()` call IS live code, but it's modeled wrong, so the dead-code tooling can't see that.\n\n2. **`name` field is no longer an identifier.** Most consumers expect `Symbol.name` to be a valid identifier (something you could write as a variable name). `\"GET event.request\"` has a space and a dot — breaks any tool that tokenizes by whitespace or treats name as a Python attribute.\n\n3. **`kind=\"function\"` is wrong.** This isn't a function definition. It's a CALL SITE that happens to make an HTTP request. If hypergumbo wants to surface HTTP-call info, the right shape is either:\n   - A new `kind` value like `\"http_call\"` or `\"external_call\"`\n   - An `Edge` (e.g., `type=\"http_request\"`) from the calling function to a route Symbol on the receiving side\n   - A `usage_context` entry (already used for inbound routes like Starlette `Route(/api/items, ...)`)\n\n4. **`origin=\"\"` ties into INV-sopon.** The HTTP linker is one of the 19 linkers identified in INV-sopon that fail to stamp `Symbol.origin`. Filing this here as additional evidence of the structural issue, though the fix can land separately.\n\n**Severity.** Medium. The miscategorization (kind=function) actively breaks dead-code analysis. The verb-prefixed names break agent consumers parsing Symbol identifiers. 17 of 18 cases are in test fixtures (lower impact), but 1 is in production code and the structural shape is wrong regardless of corpus.\n\n**Fix proposal.**\n\nThe clean fix is to NOT create `kind=\"function\"` Symbols for HTTP call sites at all. Instead:\n\n1. Emit an `Edge` of type `\"http_request\"` (or similar) from the **calling function** Symbol to either:\n   - A route Symbol on the same repo (if the URL matches one of `usage_contexts`)\n   - An external_symbol node representing the third-party endpoint\n\n2. Attach the verb / url_type / url metadata to the Edge, not a synthetic Symbol.\n\n3. If a Symbol is genuinely needed for representation (e.g., to make the HTTP call discoverable via `hypergumbo search`), use a new `kind` like `\"http_call\"` distinct from `\"function\"`.\n\nLess-intrusive interim fix: change `kind` from `\"function\"` to `\"http_call\"` and document it. Doesn't solve the deeper modeling issue but stops dead-code-maybe from flagging these as dead functions.\n\n**Test gap.** Add an assertion in `test_http_linker.py`: for every linker-emitted Symbol, `kind != \"function\"` OR `name.matches(r\"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$\")` — i.e., function-kind Symbols must have identifier-form names. Currently 18 nodes in the self-analysis fixture violate this.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/http.py` — HTTP linker (the producer)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/http.py:1319-1347` — `_create_client_symbol` referenced in INV-sopon's \"missing origin\" finding\n- `INV-sopon-...` (filed round 2) — origin field missing across 19 linkers; HTTP linker is one of them; this finding is the kind/name angle of the same overall issue\n- `INV-ronuf-...` (filed round 6) — sibling: websocket linker creates phantom file Symbols; same \"linker creates Symbols it shouldn't\" pattern\n- `INV-hosuh-...` (filed round 9) — sibling: entrypoint detection double-counts; same \"Symbol is the wrong shape for what's being represented\""  # c500
    fields:  # c500
      statement: "Symbols with kind='function' must represent function/method/closure definitions, not call sites. Symbol.name must be a valid identifier (matches the language's identifier pattern). HTTP call sites should be represented via Edges from the calling function to a route/external_symbol Symbol, not as synthetic Symbol nodes."  # c500
      root_cause: "The HTTP linker (linkers/http.py) creates Symbol(kind='function', name=<VERB> <URL>) for every detected fetch/requests/axios call site. On hypergumbo self-analysis this produces 18 such nodes including production case 'GET event.request' from packages/htrac-frontend/public/service-worker.js:54. The name field contains spaces and dots (non-identifier characters), and kind='function' is wrong (these are calls, not function definitions). Also missing origin stamp (origin=''), overlapping with INV-sopon."  # c500
